chnology stocks were leading the broad-market selloff ahead of Wednesday's open, with the Invesco QQQ ETF QQQ, +0.25% which tracks the tech-heavy Nasdaq 100 NDX, +0.33% shedding 2.4% in active trade. Meanwhile, the SPDR S&P 500 ETF SPY, -0.11% which tracks the S&P 500 SPX, -0.11% shed 1.7% premarket. Among the QQQ's most-heavily weighted components, shares of Microsoft Corp. MSFT, -0.63% shed 2.2%, Apple Inc. AAPL, -0.20% lost 2.0%, Amazon.com Inc. AMZN, +2.53% gave up 2.5%, Google parent Alphabet Inc. GOOGL, +0.66% dropped 2.1% and Facebook Inc. FB, +3.54% declined 2.6%. The QQQs had run up 7.5% over the previous four sessions, after closing Dec. 24 at a 15-month low.\n ", "external_links": ["https://smartasset.com/snippet.js"], "published": "2019-01-02T16:01:00.000+02:00", "crawled": "2019-01-02T16:09:15.031+02:00", "highlightTitle": ""}